<!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
  SEO, Open Graph, Twitter Card and schema.org metadata for a2a-rust docs.

  Notes on choices:
  - Canonical URL, og:url, and twitter:url start as seed values pointing at
    the site root and are rewritten to the current page URL by the inline
    script below. Google Search Console previously flagged introduction.html
    with "Duplicate without user-selected canonical" because every page had
    the same hardcoded canonical pointing to `/`. mdbook's Handlebars pipeline
    does not expose string-manipulation helpers, so a pure server-rendered
    per-page canonical is not feasible from a user `head.hbs` override —
    JS injection is the pragmatic fix. Googlebot and Bingbot are both
    Chromium-based and honour JS-written canonical/og:url values; pre-render
    crawlers that do not execute JS fall back to the site root, which is
    strictly better than a wrong per-page canonical.
  - Twitter card is `summary_large_image` so cards render with the full
    preview image on X/Twitter, LinkedIn, Slack, and Discord.
  - JSON-LD describes the project as a whole and legitimately uses the site
    root as its `url`, so it is NOT rewritten per-page.
  - `robots` meta includes `max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large,
    max-video-preview:-1` to permit full descriptions and large preview
    cards in SERPs.
-->

<meta name="description" content="a2a-rust: Rust SDK for the Agent2Agent (A2A) protocol, built to the final v1.0.0 spec. Build interoperable AI agents with type-safe, async Rust.">
<meta name="keywords" content="A2A, Agent2Agent, Agent-to-Agent, Rust, SDK, protocol, AI agents, interoperability, async, tokio, crates.io, multi-agent, agentic, LLM, gRPC, JSON-RPC, REST, SSE, WebSocket">
